<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Isuwa</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Isuwa, a Hurrian kingdom on the upper Euphrates, a buffer whose loyalty swung between the Hittites and Mitanni.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Isuwa lay in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elazig">Elazığ</a> plain, east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, a region rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>. It emerged as a kingdom by the 15th century BCE, inhabited by Hurrian-speaking people in the borderland between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mitanni-empire">Mitanni Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its government beyond Hittite treaties. Isuwa sheltered refugees from Hittite lands and often sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a>. Salvage excavations before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keban-dam">Keban Dam</a> flooded the plain uncovered fortified towns of the period.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i">Suppiluliuma I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> conquered Isuwa in the 14th century BCE and made it a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. After the Hittite collapse c. 1200 BCE, the region probably passed to the kingdom of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/melid">Melid</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:29.85%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hurrian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hurrian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkey</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ishuwa</dd></dl></aside></div>

